{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1793383485668,"sessionID":"ses_e72053da9ffeY5Vp446Zu901pu","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"edit","callID":"call_01a18dfc480375e7a726ce2bd8118b3b","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/kaggle/tmp/AI-Scientist-v3-main/results/revisit/opencode/20261030_163231/investigation/worker_02/ideas/10_geometry_diverse_constructive_growth_for_six_hour_revisit_compression/program_1/src/program.py","oldString":"\"\"\"Window-flexible slew-aware constellation (cycle-9).\n\nOrder of work in solve():\n 1. Build and internally verify a cap-sized Walker seed; store as best-so-far\n    before any improvement (seed-first, never-empty return).\n 2. One fast-propagation pass caches, per visibility window, a small\n    deduplicated set of interior candidate instants (buffered start,\n    quartiles, buffered end); no exact propagation anywhere in solve().\n 3. Gap-critical window-flexible scheduler: fill the largest\n    requirement-normalised edge-inclusive gap, choosing the instant that\n    minimises slew+settling cost against predecessor/successor while\n    maximising post-insertion slack. Bounded slew-safe time-shift repair\n    shifts conflicting neighbours only within their own windows, with\n    non-overlap/slew/settling/battery re-checked before any insertion,\n    plus an independent final slew/settling/battery audit.\n 4. Verified pruning: singles first, then pairs only after singles stall;\n    a smaller fleet is accepted only after a full cached requirement-exact\n    (<=0.02h epsilon) edge-inclusive re-schedule plus slew/battery audit.\nHard internal deadline at 50% of time_limit_s is checked inside every\ncostly loop; on expiry the best verified non-empty plan is returned.\nAll parameters derive from world cap/requirements/duration.\n\"\"\"","newString":"\"\"\"Geometry-diverse constructive growth constellation (cycle-10).\n\nFork of the cycle-9 window-flexible slew-aware program. Order in solve():\n 1. Build and internally verify a cap-sized Walker seed; store as best-so-far\n    before any geometry search (seed-first, never-empty return).\n 2. One fast-propagation pass caches, per visibility window, a small\n    deduplicated set of interior candidate instants; no exact propagation\n    anywhere in solve() (cached fast propagation only, reused throughout).\n 3. Score at most 4 geometry-diverse Walker families (varying plane count /\n    satellites-per-plane distribution, Walker phasing factor and RAAN\n    offset, one inclination offset and one altitude offset, all derived\n    from world cap/requirements) at a reduced fleet size by the actual\n    slew-audited scheduler's total edge-inclusive requirement-normalised\n    gap violation; keep only the best 1-2 families.\n 4. Grow a fleet bottom-up from the kept families' cached candidates:\n    repeatedly add the single satellite whose full slew-audited cached\n    re-schedule most reduces total gap violation, stopping as soon as\n    every target meets its requirement including mission edges.\n 5. Verified pruning (singles, then pairs) of the smaller of grown/seed\n    fleets; acceptance only after full cached re-schedule plus the\n    scheduler's final slew/settling/battery audit.\nHard internal deadline near 70% of time_limit_s (with earlier phase\nsub-deadlines) is checked inside every costly loop; on expiry the best\nverified non-empty plan is returned.\nAll parameters derive from world cap/requirements/duration.\n\"\"\""},"output":"Edit applied successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"diff":"Index: /kaggle/tmp/AI-Scientist-v3-main/results/revisit/opencode/20261030_163231/investigation/worker_02/ideas/10_geometry_diverse_constructive_growth_for_six_hour_revisit_compression/program_1/src/program.py\n===================================================================\n--- /kaggle/tmp/AI-Scientist-v3-main/results/revisit/opencode/20261030_163231/investigation/worker_02/ideas/10_geometry_diverse_constructive_growth_for_six_hour_revisit_compression/program_1/src/program.py\n+++ /kaggle/tmp/AI-Scientist-v3-main/results/revisit/opencode/20261030_163231/investigation/worker_02/ideas/10_geometry_diverse_constructive_growth_for_six_hour_revisit_compression/program_1/src/program.py\n@@ -1,24 +1,28 @@\n-\"\"\"Window-flexible slew-aware constellation (cycle-9).\n+\"\"\"Geometry-diverse constructive growth constellation (cycle-10).\n \n-Order of work in solve():\n+Fork of the cycle-9 window-flexible slew-aware program. Order in solve():\n  1. Build and internally verify a cap-sized Walker seed; store as best-so-far\n-    before any improvement (seed-first, never-empty return).\n+    before any geometry search (seed-first, never-empty return).\n  2. One fast-propagation pass caches, per visibility window, a small\n-    deduplicated set of interior candidate instants (buffered start,\n-    quartiles, buffered end); no exact propagation anywhere in solve().\n- 3. Gap-critical window-flexible scheduler: fill the largest\n-    requirement-normalised edge-inclusive gap, choosing the instant that\n-    minimises slew+settling cost against predecessor/successor while\n-    maximising post-insertion slack. Bounded slew-safe time-shift repair\n-    shifts conflicting neighbours only within their own windows, with\n-    non-overlap/slew/settling/battery re-checked before any insertion,\n-    plus an independent final slew/settling/battery audit.\n- 4. Verified pruning: singles first, then pairs only after singles stall;\n-    a smaller fleet is accepted only after a full cached requirement-exact\n-    (<=0.02h epsilon) edge-inclusive re-schedule plus slew/battery audit.\n-Hard internal deadline at 50% of time_limit_s is checked inside every\n-costly loop; on expiry the best verified non-empty plan is returned.\n+    deduplicated set of interior candidate instants; no exact propagation\n+    anywhere in solve() (cached fast propagation only, reused throughout).\n+ 3. Score at most 4 geometry-diverse Walker families (varying plane count /\n+    satellites-per-plane distribution, Walker phasing factor and RAAN\n+    offset, one inclination offset and one altitude offset, all derived\n+    from world cap/requirements) at a reduced fleet size by the actual\n+    slew-audited scheduler's total edge-inclusive requirement-normalised\n+    gap violation; keep only the best 1-2 families.\n+ 4. Grow a fleet bottom-up from the kept families' cached candidates:\n+    repeatedly add the single satellite whose full slew-audited cached\n+    re-schedule most reduces total gap violation, stopping as soon as\n+    every target meets its requirement including mission edges.\n+ 5. Verified pruning (singles, then pairs) of the smaller of grown/seed\n+    fleets; acceptance only after full cached re-schedule plus the\n+    scheduler's final slew/settling/battery audit.\n+Hard internal deadline near 70% of time_limit_s (with earlier phase\n+sub-deadlines) is checked inside every costly loop; on expiry the best\n+verified non-empty plan is returned.\n All parameters derive from world cap/requirements/duration.\n \"\"\"\n import math\n import time\n","filediff":{"file":"/kaggle/tmp/AI-Scientist-v3-main/results/revisit/opencode/20261030_163231/investigation/worker_02/ideas/10_geometry_diverse_constructive_growth_for_six_hour_revisit_compression/program_1/src/program.py","patch":"Index: /kaggle/tmp/AI-Scientist-v3-main/results/revisit/opencode/20261030_163231/investigation/worker_02/ideas/10_geometry_diverse_constructive_growth_for_six_hour_revisit_compression/program_1/src/program.py\n===================================================================\n--- /kaggle/tmp/AI-Scientist-v3-main/results/revisit/opencode/20261030_163231/investigation/worker_02/ideas/10_geometry_diverse_constructive_growth_for_six_hour_revisit_compression/program_1/src/program.py\n+++ /kaggle/tmp/AI-Scientist-v3-main/results/revisit/opencode/20261030_163231/investigation/worker_02/ideas/10_geometry_diverse_constructive_growth_for_six_ho